# nr-office-ooxml-pptx-charts: integration fragment

Two new modules of the crate mixdog-ooxml: `pptx_charts` (`portable/portable-pptx-charts.mjs`: add_chart, set_chart_data,
set_chart_axis, set_chart_series, set_chart_trendline / set_chart_error_bars, set_chart_data_labels) and `pptx`
(`portable/portable-pptx.mjs`: the presentation batch dispatcher over the deck, shape and chart handlers, with the targets
resolved and the slide parts renumbered after a structural operation). No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name
belongs to them.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

Add the module declarations (beside `pub mod pptx_shapes;`, keep the other tasks' lines):

    pub mod pptx;
    pub mod pptx_charts;

## Dependencies

None. The modules use mixdog-js, mixdog-office-base, mixdog-fsio, serde_json and modules of the crate; the tests use
mixdog-fonts, tempfile and mixdog-office-base (feature test-support), all already in the Cargo.toml of mixdog-ooxml.
native/core/Cargo.lock does not change.

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-pptx-base / office-pptx-deck / office-pptx-shapes (keep the list sorted by set
name), add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-charts.mjs --tree <tree>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-pptx-charts/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "07b20e4297625f95e20d82cd0c6dbf182e5837a5f9dc8a6a9767eeaeb4e79cd0",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-pptx-charts.mjs",
      "set": "office-pptx-charts",
      "totalBytes": 605843
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-pptx-charts/MANIFEST.json if the tool that keeps this file
reformats them: `node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/verify-manifests.mjs --write-index`.)

## For the task that wires the portable backend (callers of `applyPptx`)

    pptx::apply_pptx(proof, measurer, zip, operations) -> Result<Vec<Value>, String>

`proof` is a `ReadProof` (the files an operation names are read through it); `measurer` is a `text_metrics::TextMeasurer` over
the font registry (the only thing `fit_text` needs from the machine); `zip` is the loaded `zipio::Package`; `operations` is the
batch as `serde_json::Value`s. The answer is the list of what the operations reported (Node's `results`), or the message of the
first error (the operations before it stay applied in the package, as in Node). The slides are read from the package and the
slide parts renamed to their positions after a batch that moved, added, deleted, kept, duplicated or imported slides, as
`applyPptx` does. `portable-pptx.mjs` also re-exported `inspectPptxTextBoxes`: it is `pptx_core::inspect_pptx_text_boxes`.

## Not compiled

The modules and their tests were written without cargo (the wave is compiled by the lead): the first build, `cargo test -p
mixdog-ooxml` (unit tests in src/pptx.rs and src/pptx_charts.rs, tests/twin_pptx_charts.rs), is the check. The twin test replays
native/core/fixtures/office-pptx-charts and needs no Node; `twin_live_pptx_charts` (ignored) re-records through Node.
